  "source": [
    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 93276 'Frostfang Growler!' (title), 104171 (card), objective 104176; icon 28605."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter at [-84.62, 8.75, 393.1]: BJX fork FabledRealms.lua:4101 (Npcs.json Id 33936, wolf.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region None, place None."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 1 ('Frostfang Growler! (the live battle: Frostfang Growlers in Snowhill start it)'): scene sg_random_encounter_clearing, entry, exit, 5 waves, 37 spawns ({'Frostfang Howler': 1, 'Frostfang Growler': 27, 'Frostfang Prowler': 8, 'Frostfang Alpha': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Wave spots are the fork's claim of a live capture (battle 1). Zone number 1200 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_clearing has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 15 coins / 100 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "capture",
      "evidence": "rc-0136 (2026-11-11): model 176 wolf.adr, the model live sent for every Frostfang Growler (111 AddNpc rows in p12.pcap and packets_3.pcapng); 3284 wolf_generic.adr was the reference row's."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Frostfang Growler!' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Frostfang Snarlers!' (Warrior’s Cudgel of Cleaving; Wizard's Sparkle Twig of Glaciers; Medic's Reflex Hammer of Vitals; Brawler's Mallet of Rumbling), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Frostfang Snarlers!' (revision 48736), one per combat job, and 2 coins. The same pages also name Bixie Hive, Cracked Claw Caverns, Hot Springs Haven, Sheep Watch. Brawler: the wiki's 'Bell Brawler Gloves' is 'Saved by the Bell Brawler Gloves' in our record dungeons/frostfang_snarlers.json."
    }
  ]
